# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a host-registered finalizable type runs its destroy callback when
#         the last reference is dropped and the GC collects the cell.
#
# blocked: no finalizer->host-fn bridge for a script-creatable type
# matrix-row: gc-finalizer
#
# The `## host: expect-host-call <n>` directive now exists (v0.11.4-cat-f) and
# its generic host-callback-observation path is exercised by
# tests/chk/gc/expect_host_call.chk.  This fixture stays blocked on the OTHER
# prerequisite: there is no public type-registration API and no FileHandle
# binding.  Concretely:
#   - The GC finalizer hook (src/gc/ugc_incremental.c ~476/590) only calls
#     `t->destroy` off the cell's UType entry — a per-TYPE destructor, not a
#     host-fn a fixture can register and count.  Its own comment notes "no
#     concrete cell types exist, so this path is unreachable in practice".
#   - include/urbi/ exposes no urbi_register_type / UType registration symbol,
#     so a fixture cannot create a finalizable type (the FileHandle example)
#     nor route its destroy through a counting host fn.
#
# The equivalent finalizer path is unit-tested via
# tests/unit/test_ugc_finalizer.c using the internal UType + urbi_gc_alloc
# APIs directly (no chk runner, no public type-registration API needed).
#
# Activating this fixture needs a public finalizable-type registration API
# (urbi_register_type with a host destroy callback) — out of scope for the
# test-harness-only T39 work.  The generic expect-host-call mechanism is
# proven separately in expect_host_call.chk.
